1
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:15,306
‎Gyro! Something's wrong.

2
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:22,396
‎Do you hear something below us?

3
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:25,775
‎Yeah. What's making that noise?

4
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,653
‎What? What's this?

5
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:35,618
{\an8}‎What?

6
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:40,122
‎It's transformed too!
‎And it's still alive!

7
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:43,084
‎Just what is Dio's ability?

8
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:00,684
‎Get through, Johnny!

9
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:02,561
‎I flattened you too!

10
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:03,813
‎Go through the drain!

11
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,754
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

12
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:45,998
{\an8}‎#10
‎FRIGHTENING MONSTERS, PART 2

13
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:50,919
{\an8}<i>‎It was one of England's poorest villages,
‎where poverty shaped every life.</i>

14
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,422
{\an8}‎1870 ENGLAND

15
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:56,842
<i>‎There, a baby boy had just been born.</i>

16
00:02:56,843 --> 00:03:00,304
<i>‎His parents had been broken by poverty.</i>

17
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,890
<i>‎One night...</i>

18
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:11,356
<i>‎They went to the mountain,
‎dug a hole in the ground,</i>

19
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:15,193
<i>‎wrapped their sleeping baby
‎in a white cloth</i>

20
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:17,030
<i>‎and placed him inside.</i>

21
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:23,870
<i>‎They then chose to live their lives
‎as if the baby had never been born.</i>

22
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:46,391
‎Diego!

23
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:49,478
‎What? You named the baby?

24
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,854
‎Diego!

25
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:52,856
‎Stay back! He's long dead!

26
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:56,402
‎Once we're financially stable,
‎we can have all the kids we want.

27
00:03:57,028 --> 00:04:00,364
‎We'll say he was swept away by the river!

28
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:02,659
‎We made a terrible mistake!

29
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:04,910
‎We don't need money!

30
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:06,870
‎If you'd just give up drinking!

31
00:04:06,871 --> 00:04:08,956
‎What did you say? You...

32
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:12,001
‎How dare you look down
‎on your own husband?

33
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:18,341
‎Diego... Dio!

34
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:22,929
‎Dio!

35
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:30,520
‎You're drowning, you stupid woman.

36
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:35,691
‎Still, good riddance at last.

37
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:38,278
‎Both of them!

38
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:48,496
‎He's alive!

39
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:51,999
‎What a strong will to live!

40
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,458
‎I'm so sorry.

41
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:55,461
‎I'll never do it again!

42
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:57,963
‎Thank you, God.

43
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,549
‎Thank you!

44
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:05,388
<i>‎When the rain stopped,</i>

45
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:10,726
{\an8}<i>‎far downstream,
‎the mother and baby lay unconscious</i>

46
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:14,230
{\an8}<i>‎until a farm worker
‎happened to find and save them.</i>

47
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:19,443
<i>‎The mother took the surname Brando</i>

48
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:23,156
<i>‎and found work doing odd jobs on the farm.</i>

49
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,825
<i>‎By the time Diego Brando was five,</i>

50
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:31,414
<i>‎he was already working in the stables,
‎caring for horses.</i>

51
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,541
‎Dio, have you lost weight?

52
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:37,086
‎Here. Eat my share too.

53
00:05:37,628 --> 00:05:39,171
‎I'm full!

54
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:43,092
‎I've just gotten taller.
‎I haven't lost weight.

55
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:49,806
<i>‎From sunrise to sunset, they worked.</i>

56
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:52,017
<i>‎All they were given</i>

57
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:55,480
<i>‎was a place to sleep, a mug,
‎and just enough food to stay alive.</i>

58
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:00,276
<i>‎There was nowhere else to work
‎and nowhere else to go.</i>

59
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:02,612
‎Stop.

60
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:06,699
‎Don't do this... Please, don't.

61
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,536
{\an8}‎Stop!

62
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:14,206
‎Come on. I really like you!

63
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:16,666
‎Just a little won't hurt.

64
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:20,087
‎Is this how you treat the man
‎who saved your life?

65
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:23,548
‎I truly am grateful. But please stop.

66
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:26,301
‎I can't be with a married man.

67
00:06:26,302 --> 00:06:28,638
‎What would my son think if he found out?

68
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:32,266
‎You're right.

69
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:33,851
‎I'm sorry.

70
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:35,686
‎I got the wrong idea.

71
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:38,022
‎I'm truly sorry.

72
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:48,240
‎There's a hole in my mug.

73
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,325
‎Yours does too.

74
00:06:49,992 --> 00:06:52,036
‎Why? Who did this?

75
00:06:56,999 --> 00:07:00,335
‎Come on, everyone! Gather up!

76
00:07:00,336 --> 00:07:02,546
‎Time to eat!

77
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,630
‎Single file!

78
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:06,092
‎Line up in a single file!

79
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:16,853
‎My mug...

80
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,857
‎Well now, little one.

81
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:24,651
‎Looks like there's a hole in your mug.

82
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:25,944
‎What a waste.

83
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,029
‎That's one meal gone.

84
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:30,490
‎And that mug belongs to the lord.

85
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:33,160
‎You should take better care of it.

86
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:35,328
‎Someone made that hole.

87
00:07:35,329 --> 00:07:36,873
‎It wasn't me or my mom!

88
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:41,126
‎Is that so? Then who did it?

89
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:44,379
‎If you find out, be sure to tell me first,

90
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,007
‎little Dio.

91
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:51,970
‎Could you lend us two mugs?

92
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:56,349
‎Without one,
‎neither my son nor I can eat the stew.

93
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:57,476
‎Certainly.

94
00:07:57,477 --> 00:08:00,353
‎But you'll have to pay for new ones.

95
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:02,064
‎Three pounds.

96
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,235
‎We don't have that kind of money...

97
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:10,072
‎I'll repay you after next month's wages.

98
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:13,783
‎It's been five years.
‎I'll see what I can do.

99
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:18,038
‎Oh, that's right.
‎Advances on wages aren't allowed.

100
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,790
‎I'm terribly sorry!

101
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:23,668
‎Please pour the stew into this!

102
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:25,337
‎Just one serving!

103
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,631
‎That's for the livestock, boy!

104
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:31,677
‎If it smells like meat,
‎the cows and sheep won't touch it!

105
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:37,058
‎Now, I'm truly sorry,
‎but would you step aside?

106
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:40,770
‎Everyone else is waiting their turn.

107
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:54,283
‎Mom, I'm not hungry at all.

108
00:08:55,701 --> 00:08:58,328
‎I just had a great idea!

109
00:08:58,329 --> 00:08:59,788
‎I've got shoes!

110
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:02,624
‎He can pour the stew into one of my shoes.

111
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,835
‎That's a great idea--

112
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:22,103
‎Please. May I have the stew?

113
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:25,982
‎Pour it into my hands. For Dio.

114
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,234
‎It's all right.

115
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:31,112
‎Please. Into my hands.

116
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:32,905
‎Right here.

117
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:46,294
‎Don't!

118
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:50,339
‎Thank you.

119
00:09:54,802 --> 00:09:55,886
‎Mom!

120
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:59,598
‎Here, I got it for you.

121
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,141
‎Eat now, Dio.

122
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:03,351
‎Mom, let it go! Quick!

123
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:05,895
‎I'm not hungry at all!

124
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:10,066
‎No matter how poor we are,
‎never lose your dignity.

125
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:11,861
‎What about tomorrow?

126
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,323
‎The day after that?
‎And the day after that?

127
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:18,409
‎Eat this and grow big.

128
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,329
‎Grow stronger...

129
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,788
‎Grow even bigger...

130
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:26,584
‎and protect your mother, okay?

131
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:31,839
‎We'll buy new mugs next month.

132
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:34,049
‎Until then...

133
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:36,385
‎Go on. Eat it.

134
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:14,924
‎Easy...

135
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:17,885
‎Take it slow, Mom.

136
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:24,432
‎I'm sorry, Dio.

137
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,852
‎It's okay, Mom.

138
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:33,984
‎Don't be sad.

139
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:36,946
‎This is all my fault.

140
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:40,574
‎None of this is your fault.

141
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,953
‎But, Diego,

142
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:49,207
‎even the wildest horse
‎calms down when you go near it.

143
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:53,671
‎They obey you
‎and will eat from your hand.

144
00:11:56,966 --> 00:12:01,887
‎When you grow up,
‎you should ride them.

145
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:07,810
‎That's your gift.

146
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:17,194
<i>‎Dio's mother died of tetanus,
‎her life cut short at just 23.</i>

147
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:25,326
<i>‎Dio believed the burns on her hands</i>

148
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:28,204
<i>‎had led to the infection that killed her.</i>

149
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:33,085
<i>‎Instinctively, he knew
‎that man was responsible for her death.</i>

150
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:40,509
<i>‎As he grew older, Dio made vow to himself.</i>

151
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:45,264
<i>‎I'll find that man and make him pay!</i>

152
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:49,684
<i>‎And everyone on that farm
‎who turned their backs on my mother</i>

153
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:52,854
<i>‎because she'd borne a fatherless child.</i>

154
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,648
<i>‎You all abandoned my mother.</i>

155
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:58,568
<i>‎The father who abandoned us both...</i>

156
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:00,361
<i>‎The lord of that estate...</i>

157
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:01,988
<i>‎I'll never forgive them!</i>

158
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:04,783
<i>‎Every last one of them is guilty!</i>

159
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:07,285
<i>‎Ignorant country bumpkins!</i>

160
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:10,289
<i>‎I'll rise to the very top of society.</i>

161
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:13,458
<i>‎Anyone who stands in my way</i>

162
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:18,588
<i>‎will suffer an even greater humiliation
‎than eating stew from a shoe.</i>

163
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:21,926
<i>‎I'll crush their pride
‎and make them crawl!</i>

164
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:25,845
{\an8}<i>‎Victory in the Steel Ball Run race...</i>

165
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:29,683
{\an8}<i>‎It holds enough power to sway
‎even the British royal family!</i>

166
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:34,688
<i>‎I'll stop at nothing to claim it!</i>

167
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:41,904
‎This isn't the best time, but let me
‎tell you one more thing, Johnny.

168
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,198
‎It's about your left arm.

169
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:48,409
‎Those aren't letters.
‎They're constellations.

170
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:51,412
‎The letters are arranged like the stars.

171
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:55,166
‎It's the Big Dipper. The pattern matches.

172
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,335
‎And "crūs" marks the North Star!

173
00:13:57,336 --> 00:14:00,255
‎The letters are a map of the stars.

174
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:03,007
‎Match the stars to the landscape.

175
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:06,345
‎The corpse piece is on that hill!

176
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:09,848
‎Let's go get it!

177
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,450
‎Dio's back! Get farther in!

178
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:32,413
‎Get through to the other side, Johnny!

179
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:48,219
‎What the hell is Dio's ability?

180
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:51,180
‎Even the bear he devoured
‎became a dinosaur!

181
00:14:51,181 --> 00:14:53,267
‎Who knows? Just keep moving!

182
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:59,023
‎The Big Dipper formation
‎is on the cliff across the valley.

183
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:02,026
‎The corpse piece must be up there!

184
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:06,487
‎We'll descend under cover of darkness
‎and cross the valley!

185
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:10,491
‎Right. We'll get the corpse piece
‎and get out of here.

186
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:13,244
‎But, Gyro, what about our horses?

187
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:14,579
‎Dio could eat them too!

188
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:17,916
‎No. He'd never do that.

189
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:22,338
‎He's after your left arm and our lives.

190
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:27,468
‎A jockey who fought his way to the top
‎would never kill a horse.

191
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:29,803
‎I hope you're right.

192
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,652
‎Hey! What are those?

193
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:47,904
‎Tiny ones are coming in!

194
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:50,740
‎They're dinosaurs, no matter how small!

195
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,493
‎Dio sent them after us!

196
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:58,082
‎They can track movement too!

197
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:02,836
‎It peed on me!

198
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:10,134
‎They keep coming!

199
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:13,430
‎They're tracking the scent
‎of their own urine!

200
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,479
‎They're rats.

201
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:23,816
‎They reverted after they died.

202
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:27,027
‎Let's get out! More are coming!

203
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:35,493
‎What are you waiting for? Climb down!

204
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,245
‎We can't, Gyro.

205
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:39,790
‎We can't make it down.

206
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:44,503
‎There's no way we can cross the valley
‎and reach that rock formation.

207
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:53,094
‎Those are the villagers.

208
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:57,140
‎They've all already been
‎turned into dinosaurs.

209
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:59,434
‎They'll climb this cliff easily.

210
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:04,689
‎Dio can turn every person and animal
‎in this village into dinosaurs

211
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,859
‎and control them!

212
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:12,698
‎Dio's here!

213
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,782
‎Don't panic.

214
00:17:14,783 --> 00:17:16,617
‎No matter how many there are,

215
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:20,246
‎he still won't be able to see us
‎as long as we don't move.

216
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:25,251
‎But, Gyro, if Dio's trying to
‎turn the whole village into his allies

217
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:27,628
‎and take my left arm,

218
00:17:27,629 --> 00:17:32,134
‎then I think anyone wounded by Dio
‎turns into a dinosaur.

219
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:34,887
‎Even the slightest scratch...

220
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:45,439
‎What?

221
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:49,025
‎Dio scratched us back at the shack!

222
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,611
‎Both of us!

223
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:57,409
‎What did you say?

224
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:02,705
‎Dio sent more rats!

225
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:05,249
‎Stay still, Johnny! Don't move a muscle!

226
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:07,418
‎Just ignore them!

227
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:08,711
‎Are you crazy?

228
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:11,047
‎They peed on us!

229
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:14,342
‎They're following the scent!
‎They've got us locked on!

230
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:18,054
‎We'll die if we don't fight.
‎We've got to take them out!

231
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:20,348
‎No, Johnny.

232
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,725
‎Our priority

233
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:26,188
‎is to get the Holy Corpse piece
‎beyond that cliff!

234
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:30,442
‎Your transformation's slowing down
‎for some reason.

235
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:33,444
‎I'm the only one turning into a dinosaur.

236
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:37,156
‎It's because a part of the corpse
‎is inside your left arm.

237
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:40,035
‎Its holy power
‎is holding the infection back.

238
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:42,662
‎If we get the next piece,

239
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:45,499
‎it should neutralize
‎my transformation too!

240
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,297
{\an8}‎He's spotted us, Gyro!

241
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:56,300
‎I said ignore them!

242
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:57,302
‎Now!

243
00:18:57,845 --> 00:19:00,304
‎Move. Jump, Johnny!

244
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,514
‎What?

245
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:03,058
‎Run, Johnny!

246
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:13,651
{\an8}‎What are you doing?

247
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:15,153
{\an8}‎It's impossible!

248
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,197
‎It's too far!

249
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:24,204
‎Exactly. It's impossible.

250
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:28,333
‎For them, anyway!

251
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:37,426
‎Unless Dio's a flying dinosaur.

252
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:43,764
‎Dio's still sending them after us!

253
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:46,642
‎They're heading down to cross the valley.

254
00:19:46,643 --> 00:19:48,477
‎Forget Dio.

255
00:19:48,478 --> 00:19:52,440
‎Even as dinosaurs,
‎they won't be here for a few minutes.

256
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:53,525
‎More to the point...

257
00:19:57,487 --> 00:19:58,530
‎We were right.

258
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:02,700
‎Looks like we had it right.

259
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:04,244
‎This is the place!

260
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:08,456
‎The sand on the ground...

261
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:10,918
‎How? It's climbing upward from below.

262
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:15,421
‎Maybe it's reacting to your left arm.

263
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:18,883
‎No, the corpse piece is reacting
‎to another corpse piece!

264
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:23,388
‎If it's like the second stage,
‎it's really close!

265
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:34,649
‎This rock formation...

266
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,985
‎It looks just like the Devil's Palm!

267
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:40,488
‎Where is it? Where's the piece buried?

268
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,240
‎Get up here, Johnny!

269
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:44,075
‎I'm getting worse too.

270
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:46,453
‎Find it, and let's get out of here!

271
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:55,920
‎Gyro, look!

272
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:59,007
‎Up there! What's that?

273
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:04,262
‎I thought it was a statue. But it's not.

274
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,389
‎There's a hollow beneath the sand.

275
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:09,767
‎The sand's simply outlining the hollow.

276
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:12,103
‎That's energy taking shape.

277
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:14,606
‎It's the shape of a Stand!

278
00:21:15,649 --> 00:21:17,275
‎This is bad.

279
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:19,235
{\an8}‎It's taking over my mind.

280
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:21,946
‎There's something in its hands!

281
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,406
‎It's holding something!

282
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:25,700
‎That's a part of the corpse!

283
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,327
‎The next piece is the eyeballs!

284
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:31,163
‎It's holding one eyeball in each hand!

285
00:21:31,164 --> 00:21:33,416
‎Get them.

286
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:35,835
‎I'm about to become a dinosaur.

287
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:39,256
‎Johnny! If they're there, then take them!

288
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:47,514
‎-What?
‎-He pushed his own ally off!

289
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,360
‎What?

290
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:04,114
‎Dio took the eyeballs!

291
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:35,914
{\an8}‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke

